PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L08U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":8,"cefr":"B2a","unit":3,"theme":"Planning Ahead","essential_question":"How can planning today shape our future careers?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1","title":"This Time Next Year, I'll Be Preparing…: Future Continuous, Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to describe what they will be doing at a future time and what they will have done by a future time.","Students will be able to use the future perfect continuous to show how long an action will have continued.","I can say \"This time next year, I'll be studying at university.\"","I can say \"By 2030, I'll have graduated.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف ما سيكونون يفعلونه في وقت مستقبلي وما سيكونون قد أنجزوه بحلول وقت مستقبلي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المستقبل التام المستمر لبيان مدة استمرار حدث حتى وقت مستقبلي.","أستطيع أن أقول This time next year, I'll be studying at university.","أستطيع أن أقول By 2030, I'll have graduated."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"career","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪr/","definition":"the series of jobs a person has during his working life","arabic":"مسيرة مهنية","example":"She has had a successful career in medicine.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"graduate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɡrædʒəwət/","definition":"to complete your studies at a school or university","arabic":"يتخرّج","example":"My brother will graduate from university in June.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"internship","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪntɚnˌʃɪp/","definition":"a period of work, often for students, to gain experience","arabic":"تدريب عملي","example":"He did a three-month internship at an engineering company.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"specialize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈspɛʃəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study or work in one particular area","arabic":"يتخصّص","example":"She wants to specialize in children's medicine.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use the future continuous (will be + -ing) for an action that will be in progress at a particular time in the future: This time next year, I will be preparing for my exams. It is also used for planned events and polite questions about plans: Will you be using the car tonight?\nUse the future perfect (will have + past participle) for an action that will be completed before a future time. It usually comes with by (by June, by 2030, by then, by the time…): By June 2028, I will have finished school.\nUse the future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) to show how long an action will have continued up to a future moment: By the time you finish, you will have been studying for almost twenty years. State verbs use the future perfect simple: By May, I will have known him for ten years.\nwill be + -ing = in progress at a future time\nwill have + past participle = completed before a future time (by…)\nwill have been + -ing = duration up to a future time (for…)\npolite: Will you be using…? / Will you be coming…?","examples":["This time tomorrow, we'll be flying over the Red Sea.","By 2030, Riyadh will have hosted many international events.","In five years, my brother will be working as an engineer.","By the end of the month, I will have read four novels.","Will you be using your laptop this evening?","By next June, my father will have been teaching for thirty years.","The new airport will have opened by the time I graduate.","I won't be living at home when I'm at university."],"common_errors":["✗ By 2030, I will graduate. → ✓ By 2030, I will have graduated. (by + future time → future perfect.)","✗ This time next week, I will lie on the beach. → ✓ This time next week, I will be lying on the beach. (In progress at a future time → future continuous.)","✗ By June, I will have been knowing him for ten years. → ✓ By June, I will have known him for ten years. (State verb → future perfect simple.)","✗ She will have finish by Monday. → ✓ She will have finished by Monday. (will have + past participle.)"],"arabic":"المستقبل المستمر (will be + ing) لحدث سيكون جاريًا في وقت محدد في المستقبل: This time next year, I'll be preparing for my exams.\nالمستقبل التام (will have + التصريف الثالث) لحدث سيكتمل قبل وقت مستقبلي، وغالبًا مع by: By June 2028, I will have finished school.\nالمستقبل التام المستمر (will have been + ing) لبيان مدة الحدث حتى لحظة مستقبلية: you will have been studying for almost twenty years.\nنستخدم المستقبل المستمر أيضًا في الأسئلة المهذبة: Will you be using the car tonight?"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This Time Next Year, I'll Be Preparing…: Future Continuous, Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous”. Let’s learn future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U3-LS1 | This Time Next Year, I'll Be Preparing…: Future Continuous, Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “My Ten-Year Plan – Sara”: Our career counselor, Ms. Huda, asked us to imagine our lives in ten years, so I made a plan. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Our career counselor, Ms. Huda, asked us to imagine our lives in ten years, so I made a plan.","visual":"Image GV-L08-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use the future continuous (will be + -ing) for an action that will be in progress at a particular time in the future: This time next year, I will be preparing for my exams. It is also used for planned events and polite questions about plans: Will you be using the car tonight? Use the future perfect (will have + past participle) for an action that will be completed before a future time. It usually comes with by (by June, by 2030, by then, by the time…): By June 2028, I will have finished school.","on_screen":"will be + -ing = in progress at a future time • will have + past participle = completed before a future time (by…) • will have been + -ing = duration up to a future time (for…)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. This time tomorrow, we'll be flying over the Red Sea. By 2030, Riyadh will have hosted many international events. In five years, my brother will be working as an engineer.","on_screen":"This time tomorrow, we'll be flying over the Red Sea. / By 2030, Riyadh will have hosted many international events. / In five years, my brother will be working as an engineer.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “By 2030, I will graduate.” That’s not right. We say: “By 2030, I will have graduated.” by + future time → future perfect.","on_screen":"✗ By 2030, I will graduate.   ✓ By 2030, I will have graduated.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"By June, I will have finished school.\" Will school be finished in June? … Think! … Yes – before or by June. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"This time next year, I'll be studying at university.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"This time next year, I'll be studying at university.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المستقبل المستمر (will be + ing) لحدث سيكون جاريًا في وقت محدد في المستقبل: This time next year, I'll be preparing for my exams.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: By 2030, I will graduate. — الصحيح: By 2030, I will have graduated.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول This time next year, I'll be studying at university."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Ten-Year Plan – Sara","body":"Our career counselor, Ms. Huda, asked us to imagine our lives in ten years, so I made a plan.\nThis time next year, I will be preparing for my final high school exams, and I will probably be studying late every night. By June 2028, I will have finished school, and I hope I will have been accepted into a medical college.\nMedicine is a long journey. Students in Saudi Arabia usually study for six years and then complete a one-year internship in a hospital. By the time I'm twenty-five, I will have graduated, and I will have worked in several hospital departments.\nMy dream is to specialize in pediatrics, because I love working with children. In ten years, I will be working as a junior pediatrician in a children's hospital in Riyadh. I won't be living with my parents anymore, but I will still be visiting them every weekend!\nI know that my plan might change. But having a goal helps me make good choices now. By the end of this year, I will have volunteered at the Red Crescent for six months, and I will have read three books about the human body.\nWhen I told Ms. Huda my plan, she smiled. \"By the time you finish,\" she said, \"you will have been studying for almost twenty years. Make sure you enjoy the journey!\"","word_count":226,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"This time next year, I ___ for my final exams.","options":["will be preparing","am prepared","prepare","will have prepared"],"answer":"will be preparing","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By June 2028, Sara ___ high school.","options":["has finished","will have finished","finishes","will be finishing"],"answer":"will have finished","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."},{"q":"By the time she finishes, she ___ for almost twenty years.","options":["will study","has studied","will have been studying","is studying"],"answer":"will have been studying","explanation":"Duration up to a future time → will have been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام المستمر."},{"q":"___ you be using the car tonight? I need to go to the library.","options":["Do","Have","Will","Are"],"answer":"Will","explanation":"Polite question about plans → Will you be + -ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال المهذب."},{"q":"By next May, my grandparents ___ each other for fifty years.","options":["will have been knowing","will be knowing","know","will have known"],"answer":"will have known","explanation":"State verbs → future perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة."},{"q":"Engineers expect that by 2030, the new high-speed rail line ______ more than ten million passengers between the two cities.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["will have carried","has carried","carried","will be carry"],"answer":"will have carried","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the future continuous, future perfect or future perfect continuous. Word bank: will have built, will be taking, will have been working","items":[{"q":"At 9 a.m. tomorrow, I ______ (take) my driving test.","options":[],"answer":"will be taking","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By the end of the year, our team ______ (build) three robots.","options":[],"answer":"will have built","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."},{"q":"By December, my uncle ______ (work) at the hospital for twenty years.","options":[],"answer":"will have been working","explanation":"Duration up to a future time → will have been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"By 2030, I will graduate from university.","options":[],"answer":"By 2030, I will have graduated from university.","explanation":"will graduate → will have graduated. Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will graduate → will have graduated. المستقبل التام."},{"q":"This time next week, we will lie on the beach in Umluj.","options":[],"answer":"This time next week, we will be lying on the beach in Umluj.","explanation":"will lie → will be lying. In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will lie → will be lying. المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By next month, I will have been owning this bike for five years.","options":[],"answer":"By next month, I will have owned this bike for five years.","explanation":"will have been owning → will have owned. State verbs → future perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will have been owning → will have owned. أفعال الحالة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Imagine your future.","items":[{"q":"What will you be doing this time tomorrow?","options":[],"answer":"This time tomorrow, I'll be sitting in my math class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will you have achieved by the end of this school year?","options":[],"answer":"By the end of this school year, I'll have finished my first coding course.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Where will you be living in ten years?","options":[],"answer":"In ten years, I'll be living in Jeddah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How long will you have been studying English by the time you graduate?","options":[],"answer":"By the time I graduate, I'll have been studying English for twelve years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a polite question with \"Will you be…?\"","options":[],"answer":"Will you be coming to the career fair on Thursday?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Your ten-year plan.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what you will be doing in five and ten years (future continuous).","options":[],"answer":"In five years, I'll be studying computer science. In ten years, I'll be working for a technology company.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what you will have done by a certain time (future perfect).","options":[],"answer":"By 2030, I'll have graduated. By the time I'm 25, I'll have traveled to five countries.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with the future perfect continuous.","options":[],"answer":"By 2035, I'll have been programming for more than fifteen years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"This time next year, I'll be…"},{"label":"By 2030, I'll have…"},{"label":"By the time I'm 25, …"},{"label":"I'll have been working for…"},{"label":"Will you be using…?"},{"label":"When I finish…, I'll…"},{"label":"As soon as I've saved…, I'll…"},{"label":"until"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"At midnight tonight, most people in the city ___.","options":["will have slept","have been sleeping","will be sleeping","sleep"],"answer":"will be sleeping","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By the time we arrive, the guests ___ dinner.","options":["will be eating since","will have eaten","eat","have eaten"],"answer":"will have eaten","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."},{"q":"By next year, I ___ the piano for a decade.","options":["am playing","will have been playing","have been playing","will play"],"answer":"will have been playing","explanation":"Duration up to a future time → will have been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Will you be come to the meeting tomorrow?","Will you coming to the meeting tomorrow?","Are you will be coming to the meeting tomorrow?","Will you be coming to the meeting tomorrow?"],"answer":"Will you be coming to the meeting tomorrow?","explanation":"Polite question about plans → Will you be + -ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال المهذب."},{"q":"","options":["By the end of this week, I finish three chapters.","By the end of this week, I'll be finishing three chapters.","By the end of this week, I've finished three chapters.","By the end of this week, I'll have finished three chapters."],"answer":"By the end of this week, I'll have finished three chapters.","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."},{"q":"Don't call me at 7 p.m. I ___ my evening prayers.","options":["will have performed","will be performing","perform","performed"],"answer":"will be performing","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By July, Ahmed ___ his new job for six months.","options":["will have been having","will be having since","will have had","has"],"answer":"will have had","explanation":"State verbs → future perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة."},{"q":"By the time the new museum opens next spring, workers ______ on it for almost five years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["will have been working","will work","had been working","have worked"],"answer":"will have been working","explanation":"Duration up to a future time → will have been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام المستمر."},{"q":"In 2034, when the tournament begins, thousands of fans from around the world ______ into Saudi Arabia's new stadiums.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["will be streaming","stream","will have streamed by","streamed"],"answer":"will be streaming","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"Which sentence describes an action that will be finished before a future time?","options":["At noon, the workers will be painting the hall.","The workers are painting the hall now.","By noon, the workers will have painted the hall.","The workers paint the hall every year."],"answer":"By noon, the workers will have painted the hall.","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Sara at a desk with a \"Ten-Year Plan\" timeline poster: 2027 (final exams), 2028 (medical college), 2034 (graduation), 2036 (pediatrician in a children's hospital); Ms. Huda the career counselor smiling beside her. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara at a desk with a \"Ten-Year Plan\" timeline poster: 2027 (final exams), 2028 (medical college), 2034 (graduation), 2036 (pediatrician in a children's hospital); Ms. Huda the career counselor smiling beside her"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows career (the series of jobs a person has during his working life); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing career: the series of jobs a person has during his working life"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows graduate (to complete your studies at a school or university); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing graduate: to complete your studies at a school or university"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows internship (a period of work, often for students, to gain experience); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing internship: a period of work, often for students, to gain experience"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows specialize (to study or work in one particular area); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing specialize: to study or work in one particular area"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W01","script":"career. career. She has had a successful career in medicine.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W02","script":"graduate. graduate. My brother will graduate from university in June.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W03","script":"internship. internship. He did a three-month internship at an engineering company.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-W04","script":"specialize. specialize. She wants to specialize in children's medicine.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-T1","script":"Our career counselor, Ms. Huda, asked us to imagine our lives in ten years, so I made a plan. This time next year, I will be preparing for my final high school exams, and I will probably be studying late every night. By June 2028, I will have finished school, and I hope I will have been accepted into a medical college. Medicine is a long journey. Students in Saudi Arabia usually study for six years and then complete a one-year internship in a hospital. By the time I'm twenty-five, I will have graduated, and I will have worked in several hospital departments. My dream is to specialize in pediatrics, because I love working with children. In ten years, I will be working as a junior pediatrician in a children's hospital in Riyadh. I won't be living with my parents anymore, but I will still be visiting them every weekend! I know that my plan might change. But having a goal helps me make good choices now. By the end of this year, I will have volunteered at the Red Crescent for six months, and I will have read three books about the human body. When I told Ms. Huda my plan, she smiled. \"By the time you finish,\" she said, \"you will have been studying for almost twenty years. Make sure you enjoy the journey!\"","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This Time Next Year, I'll Be Preparing…: Future Continuous, Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous”. Let’s learn future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time; future perfect (will have + past participle) for actions completed before a future time; future perfect continuous (will have been + -ing) for duration up to a future time together. Listen to the start of “My Ten-Year Plan – Sara”: Our career counselor, Ms. Huda, asked us to imagine our lives in ten years, so I made a plan. Look at the green words. Use the future continuous (will be + -ing) for an action that will be in progress at a particular time in the future: This time next year, I will be preparing for my exams. It is also used for planned events and polite questions about plans: Will you be using the car tonight? Use the future perfect (will have + past participle) for an action that will be completed before a future time. It usually comes with by (by June, by 2030, by then, by the time…): By June 2028, I will have finished school. Here are some examples. This time tomorrow, we'll be flying over the Red Sea. By 2030, Riyadh will have hosted many international events. In five years, my brother will be working as an engineer. Be careful! Some learners say: “By 2030, I will graduate.” That’s not right. We say: “By 2030, I will have graduated.” by + future time → future perfect. Quick check: \"By June, I will have finished school.\" Will school be finished in June? … Think! … Yes – before or by June. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"This time next year, I'll be studying at university.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2","title":"When I Graduate, I'll…: Future Time Clauses with when, as soon as and by the time","objectives":["Students will be able to use the present simple or present perfect after time conjunctions that refer to the future.","Students will be able to choose between by and until and combine time clauses with future forms.","I can say \"When I graduate, I'll travel\" (not \"When I will graduate\").","I can say \"As soon as I've saved enough, I'll buy a laptop.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع البسيط أو المضارع التام بعد أدوات الزمن التي تشير إلى المستقبل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين by وuntil ودمج جمل الزمن مع صيغ المستقبل.","أستطيع أن أقول When I graduate, I'll travel (وليس When I will graduate).","أستطيع أن أقول As soon as I've saved enough, I'll buy a laptop."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"qualification","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkwɑləfəˈkeɪʃən/","definition":"an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill","arabic":"مؤهّل","example":"You need the right qualifications to become a pilot.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"apply","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈplaɪ/","definition":"to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university","arabic":"يتقدّم بطلب","example":"I'm going to apply for a summer job.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"employer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɛmˈplɔɪɚ/","definition":"a person or company that pays people to work","arabic":"صاحب العمل","example":"Employers look for people who can work in a team.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"salary","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsælɚi/","definition":"the money you earn every month for your job","arabic":"راتب","example":"Engineers usually earn a good salary.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"After time conjunctions (when, as soon as, before, after, until, once, by the time), use the present simple to talk about the future – not will: When I graduate, I'll travel. (NOT (not: When I will graduate))\nUse the present perfect in the time clause to show that the first action will be completed before the second: As soon as I've saved enough money, I'll buy a laptop. Once you've finished the form, send it to the office. The main clause can use any future form: will, going to, future continuous or future perfect: By the time I graduate, I'll have completed two internships.\nby = not later than (a deadline): Send your application by Thursday. until = up to that time (the action continues): I'll stay at school until 4 p.m. Comma rule: put a comma after the time clause when it comes first.\nwhen / as soon as / before / after / until / once / by the time + present simple\n+ present perfect to stress completion first\nno will in the time clause\nby = deadline • until = continues up to that time","examples":["When I finish school, I'll study engineering.","As soon as the results come out, I'll tell you.","Before you apply, read the requirements carefully.","I'll work part-time until I find a full-time job.","Once you've completed the internship, you'll get a certificate.","By the time she graduates, she'll have learned three languages.","Please submit your application by March 1.","After he's finished his training, he'll be working as a pilot."],"common_errors":["✗ When I will finish school, I'll travel. → ✓ When I finish school, I'll travel. (No will in a time clause.)","✗ As soon as I will save enough, I'll buy a car. → ✓ As soon as I 've saved enough, I'll buy a car. (Completion first → present perfect.)","✗ Submit your homework until Thursday. → ✓ Submit your homework by Thursday. (Deadline → by.)","✗ By the time she arrives, we'll finish dinner. → ✓ By the time she arrives, we'll have finished dinner. (Completed before a future moment → future perfect.)"],"arabic":"بعد أدوات الزمن (when, as soon as, before, after, until, once, by the time) نستخدم المضارع البسيط للمستقبل وليس will: When I graduate, I'll travel.\nنستخدم المضارع التام لبيان اكتمال الحدث الأول: As soon as I've saved enough, I'll buy a laptop.\nby تعني «في موعد أقصاه» وuntil تعني «حتى» مع استمرار الحدث.\nنضع فاصلة بعد جملة الزمن إذا جاءت أولًا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When I Graduate, I'll…: Future Time Clauses with when, as soon as and by the time”. Let’s learn future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U3-LS2 | When I Graduate, I'll…: Future Time Clauses with when, as soon as and by the time","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: When she gets her results, she'll call us. I won't apply until I've visited the university. What will you do after you finish school?","on_screen":"When she gets her results, she'll call us. | I won't apply until I've visited the university. | What will you do after you finish school?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"After time conjunctions (when, as soon as, before, after, until, once, by the time), use the present simple to talk about the future – not will: When I graduate, I'll travel. (NOT (not: When I will graduate)) Use the present perfect in the time clause to show that the first action will be completed before the second: As soon as I've saved enough money, I'll buy a laptop. Once you've finished the form, send it to the office. The main clause can use any future form: will, going to, future continuous or future perfect: By the time I graduate, I'll have completed two internships.","on_screen":"when / as soon as / before / after / until / once / by the time + present simple • + present perfect to stress completion first • no will in the time clause","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. When I finish school, I'll study engineering. As soon as the results come out, I'll tell you. Before you apply, read the requirements carefully.","on_screen":"When I finish school, I'll study engineering. / As soon as the results come out, I'll tell you. / Before you apply, read the requirements carefully.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will finish school, I'll travel.” That’s not right. We say: “When I finish school, I'll travel.” No will in a time clause.","on_screen":"✗ When I will finish school, I'll travel.   ✓ When I finish school, I'll travel.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"When I will graduate\" – is this correct? … Think! … No – *When I graduate*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When I graduate, I'll travel\" (not \"When I will graduate\").","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"When I graduate, I'll travel\" (not \"When I will graduate\").","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعد أدوات الزمن (when, as soon as, before, after, until, once, by the time) نستخدم المضارع البسيط للمستقبل وليس will: When I graduate, I'll travel.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When I will finish school, I'll travel. — الصحيح: When I finish school, I'll travel.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول When I graduate, I'll travel (وليس When I will graduate)."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"When I ___ school, I'll study engineering.","options":["will finish","finished next","finish","will have finished"],"answer":"finish","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"As soon as I ___ enough money, I'll buy a new laptop.","options":["have saved","saved next","will have saved","will save"],"answer":"have saved","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"By the time Sara graduates, she ___ two internships.","options":["completes","will have completed","has completed","will complete since"],"answer":"will have completed","explanation":"by the time + present, main clause often future perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"Please submit your application ___ March 1.","options":["since","until","for","by"],"answer":"by","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"I'll keep studying ___ I understand the lesson completely.","options":["for","since","by","until"],"answer":"until","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"Students who are accepted into the program ______ their first internship as soon as they complete their first year of study.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had begun","began","will begin","have been beginning"],"answer":"will begin","explanation":"Choose the future form in the main clause.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل في الجملة الرئيسة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form of the verb. Word bank: will have started, have finished, apply","items":[{"q":"Before you ______ (apply) for the job, update your application.","options":[],"answer":"apply","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"Once you ______ (finish) the course, you will receive a certificate.","options":[],"answer":"have finished","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"By the time I'm thirty, I ______ (start) my own business.","options":[],"answer":"will have started","explanation":"by the time + present, main clause often future perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"When she will get her results, she'll call us.","options":[],"answer":"When she gets her results, she'll call us.","explanation":"will get → gets. Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will get → gets. لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"You must return the library books until Sunday.","options":[],"answer":"You must return the library books by Sunday.","explanation":"until → by. by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: until → by. by أم until."},{"q":"By the time we arrive, the concert will finish.","options":[],"answer":"By the time we arrive, the concert will have finished.","explanation":"will finish → will have finished. by the time + present, main clause often future perfect.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will finish → will have finished. by the time."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Plan your next steps.","items":[{"q":"What will you do when you finish this school year?","options":[],"answer":"When I finish this school year, I'll take a summer coding course.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will you buy as soon as you have saved enough money?","options":[],"answer":"As soon as I've saved enough money, I'll buy a telescope.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you want to do before you graduate from high school?","options":[],"answer":"Before I graduate from high school, I want to visit Al-Ula.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will you have done by the time you are twenty?","options":[],"answer":"By the time I'm twenty, I'll have learned to drive.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"until\".","options":[],"answer":"I'll live with my parents until I finish university.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Career steps.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 career steps with time clauses (when / as soon as / once).","options":[],"answer":"When I finish school, I'll apply to a pharmacy college. As soon as I've graduated, I'll look for a job in a hospital. Once I've gained experience, I'll open my own pharmacy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"by the time\" and the future perfect.","options":[],"answer":"By the time I'm thirty, I'll have worked in three different hospitals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"by\" and one with \"until\".","options":[],"answer":"I'll send my application by Friday. I'll wait until the university replies.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"this time tomorrow / I / fly to Jeddah (will be)"},{"cue":"by June / she / finish school (will have)"},{"cue":"in ten years / he / work as an engineer (will be)"},{"cue":"by 2030 / they / build the new airport (will have)"},{"cue":"by next month / I / study Japanese / for a year (will have been)"},{"cue":"when / I / graduate / travel"},{"cue":"as soon as / she / save enough / buy a car"},{"cue":"before / you / apply / check your application"},{"cue":"by the time / we / arrive / the film / start"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I'll call you as soon as the plane ___.","options":["lands","will have landed","will land","landed next"],"answer":"lands","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"Once you ___ the test, you can leave the room.","options":["finished next","have finished","will have finished","will finish"],"answer":"have finished","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"By the time the guests arrive, we ___ the house.","options":["clean","will have cleaned","will clean since","have cleaned"],"answer":"will have cleaned","explanation":"by the time + present, main clause often future perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"The library is open ___ 9 p.m. tonight.","options":["since","for","by","until"],"answer":"until","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"","options":["Before you will have left, turn off the lights.","Before you leave, turn off the lights.","Before you will leave, turn off the lights.","Before you left, turn off the lights tomorrow."],"answer":"Before you leave, turn off the lights.","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"","options":["I won't decide until I've visited both universities.","I won't decide until I visited both universities tomorrow.","I won't decide by I've visited both universities.","I won't decide until I will visit both universities."],"answer":"I won't decide until I've visited both universities.","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"After he ___ his training, he'll be working as a pilot.","options":["completed next","will complete","has completed","will have completed"],"answer":"has completed","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"Applicants must send all their documents ______ the end of the month; late applications will not be accepted.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["since","during","until","by"],"answer":"by","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"When the new metro line ______ next year, commuters will save an average of forty minutes a day.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["will open","opened","will have opened","opens"],"answer":"opens","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"Choose the sentence that uses the time clause correctly.","options":["We start the meeting when everyone will have arrived.","We'll start the meeting when everyone will arrive.","We'll start the meeting when everyone arrives.","We'll start the meeting when everyone arrived."],"answer":"We'll start the meeting when everyone arrives.","explanation":"Choose the future form in the main clause.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل في الجملة الرئيسة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A university open day: Saad holding a brochure with a checklist (\"When I finish school… As soon as I get my results… By the time I graduate…\"), a calendar with \"until June\" and \"by June\" circled in different colors. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A university open day: Saad holding a brochure with a checklist (\"When I finish school… As soon as I get my results… By the time I graduate…\"), a calendar with \"until June\" and \"by June\" circled in different colors"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Planning Ahead”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will)"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows qualification (an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing qualification: an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows apply (to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing apply: to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows employer (a person or company that pays people to work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing employer: a person or company that pays people to work"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows salary (the money you earn every month for your job); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing salary: the money you earn every month for your job"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W01","script":"qualification. qualification. You need the right qualifications to become a pilot.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W02","script":"apply. apply. I'm going to apply for a summer job.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W03","script":"employer. employer. Employers look for people who can work in a team.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-W04","script":"salary. salary. Engineers usually earn a good salary.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When I Graduate, I'll…: Future Time Clauses with when, as soon as and by the time”. Let’s learn future time clauses after when, as soon as, before, after, until, once and by the time + present simple / present perfect (not will); by vs until together. Remember these patterns: When she gets her results, she'll call us. I won't apply until I've visited the university. What will you do after you finish school? After time conjunctions (when, as soon as, before, after, until, once, by the time), use the present simple to talk about the future – not will: When I graduate, I'll travel. (NOT (not: When I will graduate)) Use the present perfect in the time clause to show that the first action will be completed before the second: As soon as I've saved enough money, I'll buy a laptop. Once you've finished the form, send it to the office. The main clause can use any future form: will, going to, future continuous or future perfect: By the time I graduate, I'll have completed two internships. Here are some examples. When I finish school, I'll study engineering. As soon as the results come out, I'll tell you. Before you apply, read the requirements carefully. Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will finish school, I'll travel.” That’s not right. We say: “When I finish school, I'll travel.” No will in a time clause. Quick check: \"When I will graduate\" – is this correct? … Think! … No – *When I graduate*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When I graduate, I'll travel\" (not \"When I will graduate\").","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3","title":"Apply for a Job, Get a Promotion: Career Vocabulary and Context Clues","objectives":["Students will be able to use career collocations accurately.","Students will be able to use context clues (definition, example, contrast, cause–effect) to work out the meanings of new words.","I can say \"apply for a job\", \"gain experience\" and \"get a promotion\".","I can guess the meaning of a new word from the sentence around it."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام متلازمات المهن بدقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام قرائن السياق (التعريف والمثال والتضاد والسبب والنتيجة) لاستنتاج معاني الكلمات الجديدة.","أستطيع أن أقول apply for a job وgain experience وget a promotion.","أستطيع أن أستنتج معنى كلمة جديدة من الجملة المحيطة بها."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"colleague","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑliɡ/","definition":"a person you work with","arabic":"زميل عمل","example":"My father gets along well with his colleagues.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"promotion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/prəˈmoʊʃən/","definition":"a move to a higher position at work","arabic":"ترقية","example":"After five years, she got a promotion to manager.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"entrepreneur","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɑntrəprəˈnɝ/","definition":"a person who starts his own business","arabic":"رائد أعمال","example":"The young entrepreneur opened three cafés in two years.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"applicant","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈæplɪkənt/","definition":"a person who applies for a job or a course","arabic":"متقدّم","example":"Over two hundred applicants applied for the job.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W04"},{"word":"professional","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/prəˈfɛʃənəl/","definition":"connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well","arabic":"مهني / محترف","example":"Doctors must behave in a professional way.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W05"},{"word":"workplace","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɝkˌpleɪs/","definition":"the place where people work","arabic":"مكان العمل","example":"A safe workplace is important for everyone.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W06"},{"word":"freelance","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfriˌlæns/","definition":"working for different companies rather than for one employer","arabic":"مستقل / حر","example":"My cousin is a freelance graphic designer.","image_id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Career collocations: pursue a career; apply for a job / a course; gain / get experience; earn a salary / a living; get / receive a promotion; meet a deadline; start / set up a business; work full-time / part-time / overtime; attend an interview; have the right qualifications.\nContext clues help you understand new words. A definition clue explains the word: An entrepreneur, a person who starts his own business, … An example clue gives examples: qualifications such as a degree or a diploma. A contrast clue shows the opposite: Unlike full-time workers, freelance designers work for many companies. A cause–effect clue shows a result: Because she worked so hard, she got a promotion.\nWatch out for false friends and confusing pairs: salary (monthly pay) vs wage (pay per hour or day); employer (the company) vs employee (the worker); colleague (someone you work with) vs college (a place to study).\nCollocations/phrases: pursue a career • apply for a job • attend an interview • have the right qualifications | gain experience • earn a salary • make a living • get a promotion | meet a deadline • work overtime • start a business • work freelance","examples":["My sister wants to pursue a career in architecture.","He applied for an internship at an energy company.","Volunteering is a great way to gain experience.","She got a promotion after only two years.","We worked late to meet the deadline.","An entrepreneur, someone who starts his own business, takes many risks.","Unlike employees, freelance workers choose their own hours.","Over three hundred applicants applied for ten places."],"common_errors":["✗ I want to apply to this job. → ✓ I want to apply for this job. (apply for a job.)","✗ He won a lot of experience. → ✓ He gained a lot of experience. (gain experience.)","✗ My college at work helped me. → ✓ My colleague at work helped me. (colleague = a person you work with.)","✗ She made a promotion. → ✓ She got a promotion. (get a promotion.)"],"arabic":"متلازمات المهن: pursue a career (يسعى إلى مهنة) وapply for a job (يتقدّم لوظيفة) وgain experience (يكتسب خبرة) وmeet a deadline (يلتزم بموعد نهائي).\nقرائن السياق: التعريف، والمثال، والتضاد (unlike / but)، والسبب والنتيجة (because / so).\nانتبه: colleague (زميل عمل) وcollege (كلية)، وemployer (صاحب العمل) وemployee (الموظف).\nهذه المهارة هي أساس أسئلة Words in Context في SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Apply for a Job, Get a Promotion: Career Vocabulary and Context Clues”. Let’s learn career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U3-LS3 | Apply for a Job, Get a Promotion: Career Vocabulary and Context Clues","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. colleague: a person you work with. promotion: a move to a higher position at work. entrepreneur: a person who starts his own business.","on_screen":"colleague | promotion | entrepreneur","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Career collocations: pursue a career; apply for a job / a course; gain / get experience; earn a salary / a living; get / receive a promotion; meet a deadline; start / set up a business; work full-time / part-time / overtime; attend an interview; have the right qualifications. Context clues help you understand new words. A definition clue explains the word: An entrepreneur, a person who starts his own business, … An example clue gives examples: qualifications such as a degree or a diploma. A contrast clue shows the opposite: Unlike full-time workers, freelance designers work for many companies. A cause–effect clue shows a result: Because she worked so hard, she got a promotion.","on_screen":"career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My sister wants to pursue a career in architecture. He applied for an internship at an energy company. Volunteering is a great way to gain experience.","on_screen":"My sister wants to pursue a career in architecture. / He applied for an internship at an energy company. / Volunteering is a great way to gain experience.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to apply to this job.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to apply for this job.” apply for a job.","on_screen":"✗ I want to apply to this job.   ✓ I want to apply for this job.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we \"apply to\" or \"apply for\" a job? … Think! … *apply for* a job. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"apply for a job\", \"gain experience\" and \"get a promotion\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"apply for a job\", \"gain experience\" and \"get a promotion\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","متلازمات المهن: pursue a career (يسعى إلى مهنة) وapply for a job (يتقدّم لوظيفة) وgain experience (يكتسب خبرة) وmeet a deadline (يلتزم بموعد نهائي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I want to apply to this job. — الصحيح: I want to apply for this job.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول apply for a job وgain experience وget a promotion."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"My brother wants to ___ a career in aviation.","options":["follow up","run","chase after","pursue"],"answer":"pursue","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"She ___ for an internship at a hospital.","options":["requested","demanded","applied","asked"],"answer":"applied","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"Volunteering helps young people ___ valuable experience.","options":["gain","win","make","earn up"],"answer":"gain","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"The ___ pays its workers on the 25th of every month.","options":["colleague","employer","employee","applicant"],"answer":"employer","explanation":"Confusing pairs (colleague/college, employer/employee).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"An entrepreneur, a person who starts his own business, often takes big risks. What clue explains \"entrepreneur\"?","options":["a cause","an example","a definition","a contrast"],"answer":"a definition","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"Although Hamad had no formal ______, such as a degree or a diploma, his portfolio of designs impressed the employer so much that he was hired immediately.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["salaries","qualifications","colleagues","promotions"],"answer":"qualifications","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to its partner.","items":[{"q":"meet","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"a tight deadline","explanation":"meet → a tight deadline. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"earn","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"a good salary","explanation":"earn → a good salary. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"attend","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"a job interview","explanation":"attend → a job interview. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"start","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"a small online business","explanation":"start → a small online business. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"work","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"overtime during busy months","explanation":"work → overtime during busy months. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"get","options":["overtime during busy months","a small online business","a good salary","a tight deadline","a promotion to manager","a job interview"],"answer":"a promotion to manager","explanation":"get → a promotion to manager. Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about careers.","items":[{"q":"Which career would you like to pursue, and why?","options":[],"answer":"I'd like to pursue a career in software engineering because I love solving problems.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How can students gain experience before they graduate?","options":[],"answer":"Students can gain experience through internships and volunteering.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Would you prefer a full-time job or freelance work? Why?","options":[],"answer":"I'd prefer freelance work because I could choose my own projects.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"colleague\".","options":[],"answer":"My father and his colleagues have lunch together every Thursday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with a context clue that explains \"internship\".","options":[],"answer":"An internship, a short period of work for students, helps you learn about a job.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Career profile.","items":[{"q":"Choose a job and write 3 sentences about the qualifications and experience it needs.","options":[],"answer":"To become a pilot, you need the right qualifications. You must complete flight training. You also need to gain hundreds of hours of experience.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what makes a good colleague.","options":[],"answer":"A good colleague helps others meet deadlines. He shares ideas and respects everyone.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a contrast clue for \"entrepreneur\".","options":[],"answer":"Unlike employees, who work for a company, entrepreneurs start their own businesses.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"career","match":"the series of jobs a person has during his working life","arabic":"مسيرة مهنية"},{"word":"graduate","match":"to complete your studies at a school or university","arabic":"يتخرّج"},{"word":"internship","match":"a period of work, often for students, to gain experience","arabic":"تدريب عملي"},{"word":"specialize","match":"to study or work in one particular area","arabic":"يتخصّص"},{"word":"qualification","match":"an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill","arabic":"مؤهّل"},{"word":"apply","match":"to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university","arabic":"يتقدّم بطلب"},{"word":"employer","match":"a person or company that pays people to work","arabic":"صاحب العمل"},{"word":"salary","match":"the money you earn every month for your job","arabic":"راتب"},{"word":"colleague","match":"a person you work with","arabic":"زميل عمل"},{"word":"promotion","match":"a move to a higher position at work","arabic":"ترقية"},{"word":"entrepreneur","match":"a person who starts his own business","arabic":"رائد أعمال"},{"word":"applicant","match":"a person who applies for a job or a course","arabic":"متقدّم"},{"word":"professional","match":"connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well","arabic":"مهني / محترف"},{"word":"workplace","match":"the place where people work","arabic":"مكان العمل"},{"word":"freelance","match":"working for different companies rather than for one employer","arabic":"مستقل / حر"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We worked until midnight to ___ the deadline.","options":["meet","do","catch up","make"],"answer":"meet","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"My uncle ___ his own travel company in 2015.","options":["made up","did up","set up","put on"],"answer":"set up","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"Many students work part-time to ___ a little money.","options":["gain up","earn","win","make up"],"answer":"earn","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"Over five hundred ___ applied for the scholarship.","options":["salaries","employers","colleagues","applicants"],"answer":"applicants","explanation":"Choose the career word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"","options":["She did a promotion after three years.","She made a promotion after three years.","She got a promotion after three years.","She won a promotion of three years."],"answer":"She got a promotion after three years.","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"I study at a technical ___ in Dammam.","options":["college","colleague","collage","collect"],"answer":"college","explanation":"Confusing pairs (colleague/college, employer/employee).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"Because she always finished her projects early and helped her team, she received a ___.","options":["deadline","promotion","applicant","workplace"],"answer":"promotion","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"Doctors and lawyers are expected to behave in a ___ way.","options":["professional","profession","professionally","professor"],"answer":"professional","explanation":"Choose the career word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Unlike traditional employees who work for one company, ______ writers often work for several clients at the same time and choose their own hours.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["full-time","unemployed","retired","freelance"],"answer":"freelance","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"After her internship, Lina decided to ______ in children's dentistry because she enjoyed helping young patients feel calm.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["graduate","promote","apply","specialize"],"answer":"specialize","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A career fair in a school hall: booths for medicine, engineering, aviation, design and business; students holding application forms; a banner \"Pursue Your Passion\"; a young entrepreneur showing an app on a tablet. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A career fair in a school hall: booths for medicine, engineering, aviation, design and business; students holding application forms; a banner \"Pursue Your Passion\"; a young entrepreneur showing an app on a tablet"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows colleague (a person you work with); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing colleague: a person you work with"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows promotion (a move to a higher position at work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing promotion: a move to a higher position at work"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows entrepreneur (a person who starts his own business); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing entrepreneur: a person who starts his own business"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows applicant (a person who applies for a job or a course); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing applicant: a person who applies for a job or a course"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows professional (connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing professional: connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows workplace (the place where people work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing workplace: the place where people work"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows freelance (working for different companies rather than for one employer); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing freelance: working for different companies rather than for one employer"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W01","script":"colleague. colleague. My father gets along well with his colleagues.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W02","script":"promotion. promotion. After five years, she got a promotion to manager.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W03","script":"entrepreneur. entrepreneur. The young entrepreneur opened three cafés in two years.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W04","script":"applicant. applicant. Over two hundred applicants applied for the job.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W05","script":"professional. professional. Doctors must behave in a professional way.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W06","script":"workplace. workplace. A safe workplace is important for everyone.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-W07","script":"freelance. freelance. My cousin is a freelance graphic designer.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Apply for a Job, Get a Promotion: Career Vocabulary and Context Clues”. Let’s learn career vocabulary and collocations (pursue a career, apply for a job, gain experience, earn a salary, get a promotion, meet a deadline, start a business, make a living); using context clues to work out meaning together. Meet some new words. colleague: a person you work with. promotion: a move to a higher position at work. entrepreneur: a person who starts his own business. Career collocations: pursue a career; apply for a job / a course; gain / get experience; earn a salary / a living; get / receive a promotion; meet a deadline; start / set up a business; work full-time / part-time / overtime; attend an interview; have the right qualifications. Context clues help you understand new words. A definition clue explains the word: An entrepreneur, a person who starts his own business, … An example clue gives examples: qualifications such as a degree or a diploma. A contrast clue shows the opposite: Unlike full-time workers, freelance designers work for many companies. A cause–effect clue shows a result: Because she worked so hard, she got a promotion. Here are some examples. My sister wants to pursue a career in architecture. He applied for an internship at an energy company. Volunteering is a great way to gain experience. Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to apply to this job.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to apply for this job.” apply for a job. Quick check: Do we \"apply to\" or \"apply for\" a job? … Think! … *apply for* a job. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"apply for a job\", \"gain experience\" and \"get a promotion\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4","title":"Keep Your Tenses Consistent: Avoiding Inappropriate Shifts in Verb Tense","objectives":["Students will be able to recognize and correct inappropriate shifts in verb tense.","Students will be able to choose the verb tense that fits the time frame of a passage.","I can keep my tenses consistent in a paragraph.","I can explain when a change of tense is correct."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على التحولات غير المناسبة في زمن الفعل وتصحيحها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار زمن الفعل المناسب للإطار الزمني للنص.","أستطيع أن أحافظ على اتساق الأزمنة في الفقرة.","أستطيع أن أشرح متى يكون تغيير الزمن صحيحًا."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"career","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪr/","definition":"the series of jobs a person has during his working life","arabic":"مسيرة مهنية","example":"She has had a successful career in medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"graduate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɡrædʒəwət/","definition":"to complete your studies at a school or university","arabic":"يتخرّج","example":"My brother will graduate from university in June.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"internship","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪntɚnˌʃɪp/","definition":"a period of work, often for students, to gain experience","arabic":"تدريب عملي","example":"He did a three-month internship at an engineering company.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"specialize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈspɛʃəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study or work in one particular area","arabic":"يتخصّص","example":"She wants to specialize in children's medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"qualification","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkwɑləfəˈkeɪʃən/","definition":"an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill","arabic":"مؤهّل","example":"You need the right qualifications to become a pilot.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"apply","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈplaɪ/","definition":"to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university","arabic":"يتقدّم بطلب","example":"I'm going to apply for a summer job.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Choose one main time frame for a sentence or paragraph (past, present or future) and stay in it. An inappropriate shift changes the tense for no reason: (not: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.) → … and he got it.\nA shift is correct when the time really changes, usually with a signal: My brother worked at a bank last year, but now he works for an airline, and next year he will start his own business. Facts that are always true can stay in the present: Our teacher explained that water boils at 100°C.\nIn SAT questions, look for time signals (last year, in 1990, currently, since, by next June) and at the other verbs in the passage to decide which tense fits. Don't choose a tense because it \"sounds advanced\"—choose the one that matches the time frame.\none time frame → one main tense\nshift only when the time changes (look for a signal)\ngeneral truths can stay in the present\nSAT: check time words and the other verbs in the passage","examples":["Last summer, I volunteered at a hospital, and I learned a lot.","Every morning, my father drives to work and checks his email.","Next year, she will graduate and will start her career.","He studied law, but now he works as a journalist.","Ibn Sina wrote that the heart pumps blood around the body.","The company has grown quickly since it opened in 2018.","By the time the interview started, I had prepared all my answers.","When she gets the job, she will move to Riyadh."],"common_errors":["✗ Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it. → ✓ … and he got it. (Past time frame → past tense.)","✗ Every day, she wakes up early and went for a run. → ✓ Every day, she wakes up early and goes for a run. (Habit → present simple.)","✗ When I finish school, I studied medicine. → ✓ When I finish school, I will study medicine. (Future time → future.)","✗ In 2019, the company opens its first branch. (in a past story) → ✓ In 2019, the company opened its first branch. (Past time signal → past simple.)"],"arabic":"اختر إطارًا زمنيًّا رئيسًا للجملة أو الفقرة (ماضٍ أو حاضر أو مستقبل) والتزم به.\nالتحوّل غير المناسب: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it. والصحيح: he got it.\nالتحوّل صحيح عندما يتغير الزمن فعلًا مع كلمة دالة: … last year, but now…، والحقائق الثابتة تبقى في المضارع.\nفي أسئلة SAT انظر إلى كلمات الزمن وإلى الأفعال الأخرى في النص لتحديد الزمن المناسب."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Keep Your Tenses Consistent: Avoiding Inappropriate Shifts in Verb Tense”. Let’s learn verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U3-LS4 | Keep Your Tenses Consistent: Avoiding Inappropriate Shifts in Verb Tense","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Choose one main time frame for a sentence or paragraph (past, present or future) and stay in it. An inappropriate shift changes the tense for no reason: (not: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.) → … and he got it.","on_screen":"verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Choose one main time frame for a sentence or paragraph (past, present or future) and stay in it. An inappropriate shift changes the tense for no reason: (not: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.) → … and he got it. A shift is correct when the time really changes, usually with a signal: My brother worked at a bank last year, but now he works for an airline, and next year he will start his own business. Facts that are always true can stay in the present: Our teacher explained that water boils at 100°C.","on_screen":"one time frame → one main tense • shift only when the time changes (look for a signal) • general truths can stay in the present","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Last summer, I volunteered at a hospital, and I learned a lot. Every morning, my father drives to work and checks his email. Next year, she will graduate and will start her career.","on_screen":"Last summer, I volunteered at a hospital, and I learned a lot. / Every morning, my father drives to work and checks his email. / Next year, she will graduate and will start her career.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.” That’s not right. We say: “… and he got it.” Past time frame → past tense.","on_screen":"✗ Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.   ✓ … and he got it.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Last year, he applied, and he gets the job.\" What's wrong? … Think! … *gets* should be *got* – the time frame is past. Great job! Now you can say: I can keep my tenses consistent in a paragraph.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can keep my tenses consistent in a paragraph.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","اختر إطارًا زمنيًّا رئيسًا للجملة أو الفقرة (ماضٍ أو حاضر أو مستقبل) والتزم به.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it. — الصحيح: … and he got it.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحافظ على اتساق الأزمنة في الفقرة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"How My Uncle Became a Pilot (editing passage)","body":"When my uncle was a boy, he dreams of flying. After he finished school, he applies to a flight academy in Jeddah. The training was difficult, and he has failed his first exam. However, he doesn't give up. Today, he flew passenger planes between Riyadh and London.","word_count":47,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he ___ it.","options":["got","has got","will get","gets"],"answer":"got","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Every morning, my father drives to work and ___ his email in the car park.","options":["will check","had checked","checks","checked"],"answer":"checks","explanation":"Present habits or facts → present tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الحاضر."},{"q":"Next June, Sara will graduate, and she ___ her career in medicine.","options":["begins yesterday","had begun","began","will begin"],"answer":"will begin","explanation":"Future time frame → future forms.","explanation_ar":"الإطار المستقبلي."},{"q":"He studied law at university, but now he ___ as a journalist.","options":["had worked","works","worked","will have worked"],"answer":"works","explanation":"A correct shift signaled by a time expression.","explanation_ar":"التحول الصحيح."},{"q":"Which sentence has an inappropriate tense shift?","options":["When the manager arrived, she thanked everyone.","When the manager arrives, she will thank everyone.","The manager always thanks everyone when she arrives.","When the manager arrived, she thanks everyone."],"answer":"When the manager arrived, she thanks everyone.","explanation":"Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"In 1932, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia was officially established, and King Abdulaziz ______ its first king.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["will become","has become","became","becomes"],"answer":"became","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the correct form to keep the tense consistent. Word bank: will compete, opened, invites","items":[{"q":"In 2015, my uncle opened a small café, and two years later he ______ (open) a second one.","options":[],"answer":"opened","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Every Friday, my grandmother cooks kabsa and ______ (invite) the whole family.","options":[],"answer":"invites","explanation":"Present habits or facts → present tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الحاضر."},{"q":"Next year, I will join the robotics club and ______ (compete) in the national championship.","options":[],"answer":"will compete","explanation":"Future time frame → future forms.","explanation_ar":"الإطار المستقبلي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the inappropriate shift.","items":[{"q":"Yesterday, the interviewer asked me about my goals, and I explain my plan.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday, the interviewer asked me about my goals, and I explained my plan.","explanation":"explain → explained. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: explain → explained. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"Every year, the company hires new graduates and trained them for six months.","options":[],"answer":"Every year, the company hires new graduates and trains them for six months.","explanation":"trained → trains. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: trained → trains. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"When I graduate, I traveled to Japan.","options":[],"answer":"When I graduate, I will travel to Japan.","explanation":"traveled → will travel. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: traveled → will travel. تحول غير مناسب."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the career story.","items":[{"q":"When my uncle was a boy, he dreams of flying.","options":[],"answer":"When my uncle was a boy, he dreamed of flying.","explanation":"dreams → dreamed. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: dreams → dreamed. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"After he finished school, he applies to a flight academy in Jeddah.","options":[],"answer":"After he finished school, he applied to a flight academy in Jeddah.","explanation":"applies → applied. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: applies → applied. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"The training was difficult, and he has failed his first exam.","options":[],"answer":"The training was difficult, and he failed his first exam.","explanation":"has failed → failed. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: has failed → failed. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"However, he doesn't give up.","options":[],"answer":"However, he didn't give up.","explanation":"doesn't → didn't. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: doesn't → didn't. تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"Today, he flew passenger planes between Riyadh and London.","options":[],"answer":"Today, he flies passenger planes between Riyadh and London.","explanation":"flew → flies. Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: flew → flies. تحول غير مناسب."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with consistent tenses.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a past event with consistent past tenses.","options":[],"answer":"Last month, I attended a career fair. I spoke to an engineer. She gave me useful advice.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a daily routine with consistent present tenses.","options":[],"answer":"Every evening, my sister reviews her notes. Then she prepares her bag for the next day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a correct shift from past to present, using a time signal.","options":[],"answer":"My father worked in a bank for ten years, but now he runs his own business.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"career","clue":"the series of jobs a person has during his working life"},{"word":"qualification","clue":"an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill"},{"word":"internship","clue":"a period of work, often for students, to gain experience"},{"word":"colleague","clue":"a person you work with"},{"word":"entrepreneur","clue":"a person who starts his own business"},{"word":"professional","clue":"connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well"},{"word":"graduate","clue":"to complete your studies at a school or university"},{"word":"specialize","clue":"to study or work in one particular area"},{"word":"apply","clue":"to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university"},{"word":"employer","clue":"a person or company that pays people to work"},{"word":"salary","clue":"the money you earn every month for your job"},{"word":"promotion","clue":"a move to a higher position at work"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"In 2020, my cousin started a small business, and it quickly ___ successful.","options":["will become","became","has become","becomes"],"answer":"became","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Every day, the nurses check the patients and ___ their temperatures.","options":["record","will record","recorded","had recorded"],"answer":"record","explanation":"Present habits or facts → present tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الحاضر."},{"q":"As soon as I finish my exams, I ___ on a trip with my family.","options":["go yesterday","had gone","will go","went"],"answer":"will go","explanation":"Future time frame → future forms.","explanation_ar":"الإطار المستقبلي."},{"q":"","options":["My grandfather worked as a farmer, but now he enjoys his retirement.","My grandfather will work as a farmer, but now he enjoyed his retirement.","My grandfather works as a farmer, but now he enjoyed his retirement.","My grandfather worked as a farmer, but now he enjoyed his retirement."],"answer":"My grandfather worked as a farmer, but now he enjoys his retirement.","explanation":"A correct shift signaled by a time expression.","explanation_ar":"التحول الصحيح."},{"q":"In which sentence does the tense change for no reason?","options":["The applicants enter the room and sit down quietly.","The applicants entered the room and sit down quietly.","The applicants entered the room and sat down quietly.","The applicants will enter the room and sit down quietly."],"answer":"The applicants entered the room and sit down quietly.","explanation":"Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"","options":["Our teacher explains that the Earth orbited the Sun yesterday.","Our teacher explained that the Earth will orbit the Sun.","Our teacher explained that the Earth orbit the Sun.","Our teacher explained that the Earth orbits the Sun."],"answer":"Our teacher explained that the Earth orbits the Sun.","explanation":"A correct shift signaled by a time expression.","explanation_ar":"التحول الصحيح."},{"q":"Last week, the company announced new jobs, and hundreds of people ___ online.","options":["will apply","are applying","applied","apply"],"answer":"applied","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi worked at the House of Wisdom in Baghdad, where he ______ important books on mathematics and astronomy in the ninth century.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has written","will write","writes","wrote"],"answer":"wrote","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Each year, thousands of students from around the world apply to the King Abdullah University of Science and Technology, which ______ research in fields such as energy and water.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had specialized","specialized","will have specialized","specializes"],"answer":"specializes","explanation":"Present habits or facts → present tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الحاضر."},{"q":"By the time the new airport opens next year, engineers ______ more than one hundred new gates.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["built","will have built","had built","build"],"answer":"will have built","explanation":"Future time frame → future forms.","explanation_ar":"الإطار المستقبلي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Planning Ahead” that shows verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Planning Ahead” that shows verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) in action"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Keep Your Tenses Consistent: Avoiding Inappropriate Shifts in Verb Tense”. Let’s learn verb tense consistency in a sentence and a paragraph; justified shifts signaled by time expressions; tense in context (SAT Form, Structure, and Sense) together. Choose one main time frame for a sentence or paragraph (past, present or future) and stay in it. An inappropriate shift changes the tense for no reason: (not: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.) → … and he got it. Choose one main time frame for a sentence or paragraph (past, present or future) and stay in it. An inappropriate shift changes the tense for no reason: (not: Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.) → … and he got it. A shift is correct when the time really changes, usually with a signal: My brother worked at a bank last year, but now he works for an airline, and next year he will start his own business. Facts that are always true can stay in the present: Our teacher explained that water boils at 100°C. Here are some examples. Last summer, I volunteered at a hospital, and I learned a lot. Every morning, my father drives to work and checks his email. Next year, she will graduate and will start her career. Be careful! Some learners say: “Last year, my brother applied for an internship, and he gets it.” That’s not right. We say: “… and he got it.” Past time frame → past tense. Quick check: \"Last year, he applied, and he gets the job.\" What's wrong? … Think! … *gets* should be *got* – the time frame is past. Great job! Now you can say: I can keep my tenses consistent in a paragraph.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5","title":"Career Day: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to interview someone about his career and present their own career plan.","Students will be able to write a career plan with future forms, time clauses, collocations and consistent tenses, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can interview a professional about his career.","I can write my own career plan."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إجراء مقابلة مع شخص عن مهنته وتقديم خطتهم المهنية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة خطة مهنية بصيغ المستقبل وجمل الزمن والمتلازمات والأزمنة المتسقة، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع شخص محترف عن مهنته.","أستطيع أن أكتب خطتي المهنية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"career","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪr/","definition":"the series of jobs a person has during his working life","arabic":"مسيرة مهنية","example":"She has had a successful career in medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"graduate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɡrædʒəwət/","definition":"to complete your studies at a school or university","arabic":"يتخرّج","example":"My brother will graduate from university in June.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"internship","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪntɚnˌʃɪp/","definition":"a period of work, often for students, to gain experience","arabic":"تدريب عملي","example":"He did a three-month internship at an engineering company.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"specialize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈspɛʃəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study or work in one particular area","arabic":"يتخصّص","example":"She wants to specialize in children's medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"qualification","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkwɑləfəˈkeɪʃən/","definition":"an official record that you have finished a course or have a skill","arabic":"مؤهّل","example":"You need the right qualifications to become a pilot.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"apply","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈplaɪ/","definition":"to make a formal request for a job or a place at a university","arabic":"يتقدّم بطلب","example":"I'm going to apply for a summer job.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"employer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɛmˈplɔɪɚ/","definition":"a person or company that pays people to work","arabic":"صاحب العمل","example":"Employers look for people who can work in a team.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"salary","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsælɚi/","definition":"the money you earn every month for your job","arabic":"راتب","example":"Engineers usually earn a good salary.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"colleague","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑliɡ/","definition":"a person you work with","arabic":"زميل عمل","example":"My father gets along well with his colleagues.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"promotion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/prəˈmoʊʃən/","definition":"a move to a higher position at work","arabic":"ترقية","example":"After five years, she got a promotion to manager.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"entrepreneur","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɑntrəprəˈnɝ/","definition":"a person who starts his own business","arabic":"رائد أعمال","example":"The young entrepreneur opened three cafés in two years.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"applicant","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈæplɪkənt/","definition":"a person who applies for a job or a course","arabic":"متقدّم","example":"Over two hundred applicants applied for the job.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"professional","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/prəˈfɛʃənəl/","definition":"connected with a job that needs special training; doing something well","arabic":"مهني / محترف","example":"Doctors must behave in a professional way.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"workplace","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɝkˌpleɪs/","definition":"the place where people work","arabic":"مكان العمل","example":"A safe workplace is important for everyone.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"freelance","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfriˌlæns/","definition":"working for different companies rather than for one employer","arabic":"مستقل / حر","example":"My cousin is a freelance graphic designer.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: the future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, context clues and consistent tenses.\nA career plan moves through time: what you are doing now, what you will be doing at certain points, and what you will have achieved by certain dates. Keep each part in its correct time frame, and use transitions (first, after that, by then, as a result, however) to connect the steps logically.\n✔ will be doing (at a future time) • will have done (by a future time)\n✔ when / as soon as / by the time + present\n✔ pursue a career, gain experience, apply for, get a promotion\n✔ consistent tenses – shift only when the time changes","examples":["In five years, I will be working in a research lab.","By 2032, I will have completed my master's degree.","When I finish university, I'll apply for a job at Aramco.","As soon as I've gained enough experience, I'll start my own business.","By the time I'm thirty, I will have worked in three countries.","I want to pursue a career in renewable energy.","Last year, I attended a coding camp, and I loved it.","My plan may change; however, my goal will stay the same."],"common_errors":["✗ When I will finish university, I'll apply for a job. → ✓ When I finish university, I'll apply for a job. (No will in a time clause.)","✗ By 2032, I will complete my degree. → ✓ By 2032, I will have completed my degree. (by + future time → future perfect.)","✗ Last year, I attended a camp, and I love it. → ✓ Last year, I attended a camp, and I loved it. (Keep the past time frame.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المستقبل المستمر والمستقبل التام وجمل الزمن المستقبلية ومتلازمات المهن واتساق الأزمنة.\nالخطة المهنية تتحرك عبر الزمن: ماذا تفعل الآن، وماذا ستكون تفعل، وماذا ستكون قد أنجزت بحلول تواريخ محددة.\nاستخدم روابط مثل first وafter that وby then وhowever لربط الخطوات منطقيًّا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Career Day: Language in Use”. Let’s learn future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U3-LS5 | Career Day: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Career Day interviews: in pairs, one student plays a professional (doctor, engineer, pilot, entrepreneur, teacher) and the other interviews him (past experience, present job, future plans). Then swap roles and report one interesting answer to the class.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: the future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, context clues and consistent tenses. A career plan moves through time: what you are doing now, what you will be doing at certain points, and what you will have achieved by certain dates. Keep each part in its correct time frame, and use transitions (first, after that, by then, as a result, however) to connect the steps logically.","on_screen":"✔ will be doing (at a future time) • will have done (by a future time) • ✔ when / as soon as / by the time + present • ✔ pursue a career, gain experience, apply for, get a promotion","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. In five years, I will be working in a research lab. By 2032, I will have completed my master's degree. When I finish university, I'll apply for a job at Aramco.","on_screen":"In five years, I will be working in a research lab. / By 2032, I will have completed my master's degree. / When I finish university, I'll apply for a job at Aramco.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will finish university, I'll apply for a job.” That’s not right. We say: “When I finish university, I'll apply for a job.” No will in a time clause.","on_screen":"✗ When I will finish university, I'll apply for a job.   ✓ When I finish university, I'll apply for a job.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “By 2032, I will complete my degree.”? … Think! … It should be “By 2032, I will have completed my degree.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview a professional about his career.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can interview a professional about his career.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المستقبل المستمر والمستقبل التام وجمل الزمن المستقبلية ومتلازمات المهن واتساق الأزمنة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When I will finish university, I'll apply for a job. — الصحيح: When I finish university, I'll apply for a job.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع شخص محترف عن مهنته."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam","body":"Last week, my uncle Ziyad visited our school for Career Day.\nHe has been working as an aerospace engineer for twelve years, and next month he will be starting a new project on satellites.\nWhen he was my age, he didn't know what career he wanted to pursue; however, he loved building model planes.\nHe told us that by the time he graduated, he had already completed two internships.\n\"As soon as you find something you love, start learning everything about it,\" he advised.\nBy 2030, his team will have launched three satellites, and he will be leading the team that controls them.\nI've decided that when I finish school, I will apply to study engineering too.","word_count":117,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's report. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam's uncle visited the school for Career Day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His uncle has been working as an engineer for twenty years.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"As a boy, his uncle loved building model planes.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His uncle completed his internships after he graduated.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"By 2030, his team will have launched three satellites.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam has decided to study medicine.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Career Day: My Uncle the Engineer – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Next month, Adam's uncle ___ a new project on satellites.","options":["will be starting","starts yesterday","will have started since","started"],"answer":"will be starting","explanation":"Future continuous or future perfect.","explanation_ar":"صيغ المستقبل."},{"q":"By 2030, his team ___ three satellites.","options":["has launched","will be launch","launches","will have launched"],"answer":"will have launched","explanation":"Future continuous or future perfect.","explanation_ar":"صيغ المستقبل."},{"q":"When he was Adam's age, he didn't know what career he wanted to ___.","options":["run","follow up","pursue","chase up"],"answer":"pursue","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"When I ___ school, I will apply to study engineering.","options":["finish","finished next","will have finished","will finish"],"answer":"finish","explanation":"Future time clause.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن."},{"q":"","options":["He completes two internships and then got his first job.","He will complete two internships and then got his first job.","He completed two internships and then got his first job.","He completed two internships and then gets his first job."],"answer":"He completed two internships and then got his first job.","explanation":"Tense consistency.","explanation_ar":"اتساق الأزمنة."},{"q":"As a boy, Ziyad did not know which career to choose. ______ he loved building model planes, and that hobby eventually led him to engineering.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","However,","Therefore,","Similarly,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Career Day interview. Write your notes.","items":[{"q":"Question about the past: ___","options":[],"answer":"What did you study at university?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question about the present: ___","options":[],"answer":"What does a typical day at work look like?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question about the future (future continuous or future perfect): ___","options":[],"answer":"What will you be working on next year?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The most interesting answer you heard: ___","options":[],"answer":"He said that by 2030, his team will have launched three satellites.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"One piece of advice you got: ___","options":[],"answer":"He told us to gain experience through internships before we graduate.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your career plan.","items":[{"q":"Plan: your dream career, steps (school, university, internship, first job), dates, future continuous, future perfect, time clauses.","options":[],"answer":"renewable energy engineer; finish school 2028; study engineering; internship 2031; graduate 2032; working for a solar company by 2035","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your career plan in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"My dream is to pursue a career in renewable energy. When I finish school in 2028, I'll apply to study electrical engineering. By 2031, I will have completed an internship at a solar power company. As soon as I graduate, I'll look for a full-time job. In 2035, I'll be working as an engineer on large solar farms. By the time I'm thirty, I will have gained experience in several countries. I may change some details of my plan; however, I'll always keep my goal in mind. I believe hard work and clear goals will help me succeed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: future forms? no will after when / as soon as? consistent tenses? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"When I will finish school\" to \"When I finish school\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"career","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"graduate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"internship","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"specialize","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"qualification","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"apply","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"employer","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"salary","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"colleague","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"promotion","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"entrepreneur","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"applicant","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"professional","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"workplace","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"freelance","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"In ten years, I ___ as a software engineer, I hope.","options":["will be working","worked","will have worked since","work"],"answer":"will be working","explanation":"Future continuous or future perfect.","explanation_ar":"صيغ المستقبل."},{"q":"By the end of my internship, I ___ in three departments.","options":["have been worked","will have worked","work","will be work"],"answer":"will have worked","explanation":"Future continuous or future perfect.","explanation_ar":"صيغ المستقبل."},{"q":"As soon as I ___ my degree, I'll start my own business.","options":["have finished","finished next","will have finished","will finish"],"answer":"have finished","explanation":"Future time clause.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن."},{"q":"She hopes to ___ a good salary after she graduates.","options":["win","make up","earn","gain up"],"answer":"earn","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"Last year, my sister applied for a scholarship, and she ___ it.","options":["has won","wins","will win","won"],"answer":"won","explanation":"Tense consistency.","explanation_ar":"اتساق الأزمنة."},{"q":"The young entrepreneur's app became popular very quickly. ______ she hired ten new employees within six months.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["However,","In contrast,","Nevertheless,","As a result,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Many people think that engineers only work in offices. ______ many engineers spend most of their time at construction sites, factories or laboratories.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","For this reason,","In reality,","In addition,"],"answer":"In reality,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Ibn Sina studied medicine as a teenager.\n• By the age of eighteen, he was already a respected doctor.\n• He wrote The Canon of Medicine.\n• The book was used in Europe for centuries.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize how early Ibn Sina's career began. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Ibn Sina began studying medicine as a teenager and was already a respected doctor by the age of eighteen.","The Canon of Medicine was used in Europe for centuries.","Ibn Sina's book was used for a long time.","Ibn Sina wrote a famous book called The Canon of Medicine."],"answer":"Ibn Sina began studying medicine as a teenager and was already a respected doctor by the age of eighteen.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Internships give students real work experience.\n• Many employers prefer applicants with experience.\n• Some internships are paid; others are not.\n• Internships often last between one and six months.\n\nThe student wants to explain why internships can help students get jobs. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Students can do internships, which are sometimes paid.","Because many employers prefer applicants with experience, internships can give students an advantage when they apply for jobs.","Some internships are paid, while others are not.","Internships often last between one and six months."],"answer":"Because many employers prefer applicants with experience, internships can give students an advantage when they apply for jobs.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a career plan:","options":["By the time I'm twenty-five, I will graduate, and I working at an engineering company.","By the time I'm twenty-five, I graduated, and I'll be work at an engineering company.","By the time I'm twenty-five, I will have graduated, and I'll be working at an engineering company.","By the time I will be twenty-five, I graduate, and I worked at an engineering company."],"answer":"By the time I'm twenty-five, I will have graduated, and I'll be working at an engineering company.","explanation":"Future continuous or future perfect.","explanation_ar":"صيغ المستقبل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Career Day in the school hall: Adam interviewing his uncle Ziyad, an aerospace engineer, who is holding a small satellite model; posters about different careers on the walls. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Career Day in the school hall: Adam interviewing his uncle Ziyad, an aerospace engineer, who is holding a small satellite model; posters about different careers on the walls"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Planning Ahead”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Planning Ahead”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L08-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS5-T1","script":"Last week, my uncle Ziyad visited our school for Career Day. He has been working as an aerospace engineer for twelve years, and next month he will be starting a new project on satellites. When he was my age, he didn't know what career he wanted to pursue; however, he loved building model planes. He told us that by the time he graduated, he had already completed two internships. \"As soon as you find something you love, start learning everything about it,\" he advised. By 2030, his team will have launched three satellites, and he will be leading the team that controls them. I've decided that when I finish school, I will apply to study engineering too.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Career Day: Language in Use”. Let’s learn future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, tense consistency; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Career Day interviews: in pairs, one student plays a professional (doctor, engineer, pilot, entrepreneur, teacher) and the other interviews him (past experience, present job, future plans). Then swap roles and report one interesting answer to the class. Today you use all of Unit 3: the future continuous and future perfect, future time clauses, career collocations, context clues and consistent tenses. A career plan moves through time: what you are doing now, what you will be doing at certain points, and what you will have achieved by certain dates. Keep each part in its correct time frame, and use transitions (first, after that, by then, as a result, however) to connect the steps logically. Here are some examples. In five years, I will be working in a research lab. By 2032, I will have completed my master's degree. When I finish university, I'll apply for a job at Aramco. Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will finish university, I'll apply for a job.” That’s not right. We say: “When I finish university, I'll apply for a job.” No will in a time clause. Quick check: what is wrong with “By 2032, I will complete my degree.”? … Think! … It should be “By 2032, I will have completed my degree.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview a professional about his career.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"This time next month, we ___ on our school trip to Al-Ula.","options":["traveled","will have traveled since","will be traveling","travel"],"answer":"will be traveling","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"By the end of the year, the company ___ fifty new employees.","options":["will have hired","has hired","will be hire","hires"],"answer":"will have hired","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."},{"q":"By 2030, my father ___ as a pilot for twenty-five years.","options":["will have been flying","has been flying","is flying","will fly"],"answer":"will have been flying","explanation":"Duration up to a future time → will have been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام المستمر."},{"q":"___ you be using the printer this afternoon?","options":["Are","Do","Will","Have"],"answer":"Will","explanation":"Polite question about plans → Will you be + -ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال المهذب."},{"q":"By next week, I ___ my new phone for a year.","options":["will be having","have","will have been having","will have had"],"answer":"will have had","explanation":"State verbs → future perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة."},{"q":"When the new hospital ___, it will employ over two thousand people.","options":["will have opened","opens","opened next","will open"],"answer":"opens","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"As soon as I ___ my homework, I'll call you.","options":["have finished","will finish","will have finished","finished next"],"answer":"have finished","explanation":"Completion first → present perfect in the time clause.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام للاكتمال."},{"q":"By the time we reach the airport, the plane ___.","options":["will leave since","will have left","has left","leaves"],"answer":"will have left","explanation":"by the time + present, main clause often future perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"Please return the completed forms ___ Thursday.","options":["for","by","until","since"],"answer":"by","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"We will keep working ______ every member of the team understands the new system; only then will we move on to the next stage.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["until","during","by","since"],"answer":"until","explanation":"by (deadline) vs until (up to that time).","explanation_ar":"by أم until."},{"q":"My brother wants to ___ a career in law.","options":["chase after","follow up","run","pursue"],"answer":"pursue","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"She ___ for a job at the new museum.","options":["demanded","requested","applied","asked"],"answer":"applied","explanation":"Career collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة المهن."},{"q":"The ___ asked me many questions during the interview.","options":["employee","employer","colleague","applicant"],"answer":"employer","explanation":"Confusing pairs (colleague/college, employer/employee).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"Although many people think of him as a famous scientist, Al-Biruni was also a skilled ______, a person who studies and writes about history.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["entrepreneur","applicant","historian","colleague"],"answer":"historian","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"Because she had always finished her work on time and trained new staff, she was given a ___ to team leader.","options":["workplace","deadline","promotion","salary"],"answer":"promotion","explanation":"Use the context clue to find the meaning.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"Last week, my cousin passed his driving test, and he ___ very happy.","options":["was","has been","will be","is"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"Every night, my mother reads the news and ___ a cup of tea.","options":["had drunk","will drink","drank","drinks"],"answer":"drinks","explanation":"Present habits or facts → present tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الحاضر."},{"q":"Find the sentence with an unnecessary shift in tense.","options":["The manager always smiles at the end of an interview.","After the interview ended, the manager smiled at me.","When the interview ends, the manager will smile at me.","After the interview ended, the manager smiles at me."],"answer":"After the interview ended, the manager smiles at me.","explanation":"Inappropriate tense shift → correct it.","explanation_ar":"تحول غير مناسب."},{"q":"In 1938, oil was discovered in commercial quantities in Dammam, and the discovery ______ the economy of Saudi Arabia forever.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["changed","will change","has changed","changes"],"answer":"changed","explanation":"Past time frame → past tenses.","explanation_ar":"الإطار الماضي."},{"q":"","options":["My aunt taught math for twenty years, but now she wrote children's books.","My aunt taught math for twenty years, but now she writes children's books.","My aunt teaches math for twenty years, but now she wrote children's books.","My aunt will teach math for twenty years, but now she writes children's books."],"answer":"My aunt taught math for twenty years, but now she writes children's books.","explanation":"A correct shift signaled by a time expression.","explanation_ar":"التحول الصحيح."},{"q":"Many young Saudis are starting their own companies. ______ the number of small businesses in the Kingdom has grown quickly in recent years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["In contrast,","Instead,","However,","As a result,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Saudi Vision 2030 was launched in 2016.\n• One of its goals is to create more jobs for young people.\n• It supports small and medium-sized businesses.\n• It encourages entrepreneurship.\n\nThe student wants to explain how Vision 2030 helps young people's careers. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Small and medium-sized businesses exist in Saudi Arabia.","Saudi Vision 2030 was launched in 2016.","Vision 2030 is a plan that was launched by Saudi Arabia.","By supporting small businesses and encouraging entrepreneurship, Vision 2030 aims to create more jobs for young people."],"answer":"By supporting small businesses and encouraging entrepreneurship, Vision 2030 aims to create more jobs for young people.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"when i will graduate, i work for a big company.\"","options":["When I will graduate, I will work for a big company.","When I graduate, I worked for a big company.","When I graduate, I will work for a big company.","when I graduate, I will work for a big company."],"answer":"When I graduate, I will work for a big company.","explanation":"Time clause → present simple, not will.","explanation_ar":"لا will في جملة الزمن."},{"q":"\"By 2030, she will have opened her own clinic.\" When will the clinic open?","options":["It is open now.","before or by 2030","after 2030","in 2040"],"answer":"before or by 2030","explanation":"Completed before a future time → will have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل التام."}],"theme_ar":"التخطيط للمستقبل","essential_question_ar":"كيف يمكن للتخطيط اليوم أن يشكّل مهننا المستقبلية؟","can_do":"I can describe future plans with the future continuous, future perfect and future perfect continuous, use future time clauses correctly, talk about careers with precise collocations, and keep verb tenses consistent.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف خططي المستقبلية بالمستقبل المستمر والمستقبل التام والمستقبل التام المستمر، وأستخدم جمل الزمن المستقبلية بشكل صحيح، وأتحدث عن المهن بمتلازمات دقيقة، وأحافظ على اتساق أزمنة الأفعال."});
